  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is to test the full-capability multimodal pipeline: multimodal (RNA+image), multiprofile with transformer aggregation, scgpt RNA encoder, and ViT-L image encoder with weighted fusion. This establishes the performance ceiling and simultaneously tests whether the combination of strong encoders, multiprofile aggregation, and multimodal fusion is viable. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components (e.g., replace scgpt with PCA, ViT-L with ResNet50, transformer with avgpool) to find cheaper configurations that match its accuracy. If it underperforms, it reveals which architectural choice is limiting. Expected relative cost: HIGH — this is the most expensive configuration in the set (scgpt foundation model + ViT-L + transformer aggregation + multiprofile processing), but as the single most informative experiment to anchor the search, the cost is justified given 9 remaining experiments to explore cheaper alternatives."
}

